.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt LCC-PANELS 1
.Os @PROJECT_VERSION@

.Sh NAME
.Nm lcc-panels
.Nd configure Lumina desktop panels and panel plugins.

.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | -help
.Op Fl v | -version
.Op Fl s | -screen Ar number

.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is part of the Lumina Control Center.
It manages the panels on one screen.
Panels can be added and removed.
For each panel the screen edge and alignment, thickness in pixels, length as
a percentage of the screen edge, a custom color, and auto-hide can be set.
Panel plugins can be added, removed and reordered, including launchers for
specific applications and custom scripts.
Predefined panel profiles can be applied as a starting point.

.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display help on command line options.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Display version information.
.It Fl s Ar number , Fl -screen Ar number
Configure the panels on screen
.Ar number ,
counted from 0.
The default is 0.
.Nm
exits with an error if the screen does not exist.
The screen can also be changed from within the window.
.El

.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl % lcc-panels -s 1
Configure the panels on the second monitor.

.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/lcc-panels
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lumina-desktop/desktopsettings.conf
Panel settings shared with
.Xr lumina-desktop 1 .
.El

.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lcc 1 ,
.Xr lcc-desktop 1 ,
.Xr lcc-menu 1 ,
.Xr lumina-desktop 1

